WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:01.950
What?

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.750
What’s going on?

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:03.690
What’s that?

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.200
What happened?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.650
Cleaning!

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.700
That’s a noisy junk robot!

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.170
Cleaning...

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.410
What’s going on?

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.040
What about my demands?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.020
Don’t you care what happens to them?

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.220
Get my money ready!

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.960
And a helicopter!

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:38.020
The criminal has barricaded himself in the shopping mall
and is demanding money and a helicopter.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.870
Oh no! It’s a crime!

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.890
Yuma!

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.560
I know you’re at the shopping mall!

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.800
What are you talking about?

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.970
I’m... umm... at school!

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.040
Yuma!

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.210
It’s fine.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.140
Yuma!

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:56.990
Yes?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.740
I know where you are!

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.410
You’re on TV!

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:06.320
I’m on TV!

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.590
Listen! Get footage for a scoop!

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.290
Even though you say that...

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:13.550
Sheesh.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.760
Other than a helicopter...

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.510
Hurry up and bring it!

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.880
He looks scary.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.910
Look, Yuma.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.440
It’s a Number.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.110
The criminal is a Number?

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.280
Excuse me!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.610
Yuma!

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.600
Number confirmed.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.260
Let’s begin the hunt.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.580
Understood!

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.590
Sorry!

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.580
What’s that?

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.850
Where’s my money?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.570
Ouch!

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.100
What?

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.570
What’s going on?

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.560
Time has stopped!

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.540
Why?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.430
What’s going on?

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.660
What’s happening?

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.350
Who are you?

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.350
I’m the light that shines
on the shadows inside a person’s heart.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.320
People call me the Number Hunter.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.030
Number Hunter?

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.530
I’m going to take your Number!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.200
How dare you hurt my friend!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.620
Let’s beat him up, buddy!

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.090
No, I mean Master Kaito!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.050
Let’s duel!

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.900
I’ll expose your darkness!

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.510
A duel?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.470
Yeah. Numbers only possess duelists.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.470
I see. This card is called a Number.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.440
So you must also have this card.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.930
Interesting!

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.900
I’m going to take your Number instead!

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.320
You fool. I’ll finish you quickly!

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.950
Understood!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.410
Duel mode! Photon change!

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.180
I’m going to hunt your soul!

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.300
Move out of the way!

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.050
Yuma, they started a duel up there.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.250
What’s going on?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.700
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.820
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.740
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:34.000
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:41.380
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.920
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:54.480
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.360
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.480
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.330
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.660
Everyone is not the same

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.580
That’s the reason for living

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.840
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:22.260
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.510
I travel to the edge of the world

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:29.970
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.810
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.060
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.440
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.110
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:52.090
Who are you?

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.990
What are you?

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:59.080
Your Number’s power has reached its limit.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:01.960
\hThe Soul Hunter! The Number Hunter Appears!\h

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:01.960
Number 13:

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.500
Go, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.840
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.060
Photon Hand.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.420
Number retrieval complete.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.210
Understood!

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.100
What’s this?

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.860
Why is the criminal knocked out?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.560
Number Hunter...

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.290
What’s he talking about?

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.030
Number Hunter?

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.570
Can it be?

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:11.700
What’s this?

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.660
Someone took his Number?

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.420
That’s who we saw.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.880
Who’s that boy?

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.800
Seize him!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.100
Who is he?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.950
How did you get in?

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:36.950
Don’t struggle!

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.100
Wait a second!

00:07:51.240 --> 00:08:01.870
Garbage... Garbage...

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:26.550
Let me hear more screams!

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.950
More! More!

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:10.990
Enter.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:18.410
Are you retrieving Numbers easily?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.700
Yes.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:23.040
That’s wonderful!

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:29.590
Your passionate dueling will bring peace to Heartland City.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:33.270
How many Numbers have you collected?

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:34.340
Orbital.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.590
Understood!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:41.060
We’ve collected 11 Number Cards.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:44.280
Fantastic!

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:48.830
I knew you’d collect so many
in a short amount of time.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:52.770
What’s wrong, Kaito?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.930
I know.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:59.160
You’re worried about the souls you’ve captured.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:02.130
It’s unavoidable.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:08.650
With our current scientific knowledge,
when we take a Number, we also take his soul.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.010
But don’t worry.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:19.550
People who use Numbers are villains whose
evil desires grow when they’re possessed.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:24.130
Is it true that if I collect
100 Number Cards, Haruto will be...

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.560
My younger brother will return to normal?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.230
Of course!

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:33.730
The only way to cure Haruto
is to collect the Numbers.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.970
You must believe that.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:37.970
Don’t worry.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.990
I’ll inform Dr. Faker about your passion.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.290
Okay.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:48.080
Continue searching for Numbers.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:53.090
That will cure Haruto quicker.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:11.440
What are the results for retrieving Numbers?

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.350
Dr. Faker, everything is proceeding smoothly.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.820
I see. That’s good.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:24.870
People always throw away something to protect what’s important.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:30.040
Just like how I threw away humanity in order to protect this world.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:35.500
In order to protect Kaito and Haruto,
I threw away humans.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.960
Yes, Dr. Faker.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:42.680
I knew that an envoy
from the Astral World would come someday.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:48.420
Clearly, that the envoy arrived
on that day at that time.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.060
Crush him until there’s nothing left!

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:57.020
Send his remains back to his world!

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.780
That’s the only way to protect our world!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:01.830
Agreed!

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.990
Regarding the shopping mall hostage crisis...

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:11.960
The boy detained in this video suddenly
appeared between the criminal and the police...

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.210
You became the scoop?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:20.170
Before I knew it, Yuma entered the crime scene.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.040
But how?

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:25.220
Don’t sweat the details.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.430
Yuma.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.390
You’re not going to tell them
about the Numbers?

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.780
You fool!

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:34.350
My sister doesn’t allow me to duel.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.650
I can’t tell her—

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.060
What?

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.110
It’s nothing.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.290
Don’t tell me you’re—

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.930
No! I’m not dueling!

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.820
Number Hunter...

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:06.970
Thank you!

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:24.990
Big brother...

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:28.170
Haruto, how do you feel?

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.490
Big brother...

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.450
What is it?

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.390
Why is everyone laughing?

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:38.670
I don’t need the sound of laughter.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.450
I need screams.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.670
That calms me down.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.590
I need more screams.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.570
Haruto...

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.830
Big brother, am I weird?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:59.520
No, you’re just having a bad dream.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.140
Dream?

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:03.970
Yeah, a bad dream.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.910
But don’t worry.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:09.720
I promise to wake you from that dream.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.420
Yuma.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:18.920
What is it?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:23.420
If there’s someone else
who’s collecting Numbers...

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.910
You mean the Number Hunter?

00:14:25.910 --> 00:14:30.890
That means the hunter
may someday come for me.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:35.210
It won’t be long until the hunter finds you.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.890
Actually, he may already know about you.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.880
What? Are you scared?

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:44.730
In that case, I’ll beat him in a duel for you.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.070
I have a bad feeling.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:57.500
They built a large duel field in the neighboring city.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.400
That’s awesome!

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.400
Let’s go next Sunday!

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:02.460
Right, Kotori?

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.800
I’ll show you my kattobing!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.850
I’ll watch if you’re going to win.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.350
I was so close.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.930
If my attack succeeded at that moment...

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.450
Right, Kotori?

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:22.820
You lost all your matches.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.440
C’mon!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:27.090
Kattobing means to keep trying!

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.030
It’s important to never give up!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.560
When are you going to win?

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:32.060
I’ll win next time!

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:32.940
Yuma.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.440
You need to be careful.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.340
I have a bad feeling.

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:40.470
You’re talking about that again?

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:41.540
What’s wrong?

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.750
It’s nothing.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.010
Rain?

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.440
Oh no! It’s starting to rain!

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.510
Let’s go, Kotori!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.860
Yuma!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.390
Hurry up, Kotori!

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.330
Wait up!

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:03.000
Kotori!

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.680
Yuma... Yuma!

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.950
What’s this?

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:19.910
Kotori!

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:25.990
What’s going on?

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.630
It’s the same as before.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.090
That whistle!

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:33.590
Can it be?

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.860
Who are you?

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.860
Is this your doing?

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:55.810
There’s a special field in this area right now.

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:58.530
Time moves at 1/10,000 the speed.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.250
It’s Orbital 7’s power.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:07.000
Only people with Numbers can move in this area.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.390
Like I thought, you have a Number.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.300
Number? Can it be?

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.920
Number Hunter?

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.230
Yuma, he’s dangerous! Run away!

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:18.430
Run away?

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.020
What’s this?

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:27.980
Due to this Duel Anchor, until our duel ends...

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.920
...we can’t separate!

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:32.690
What?

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:36.920
In other words, you can’t escape from this duel.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:39.410
I will hunt your Number!

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:43.870
I don’t know who you are,
but I always accept a challenge!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.370
Yuma, I’ll also help in this duel.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.000
What are you talking about?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.790
You were scared until now!

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.840
I don’t believe in intuition.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.310
But I’m making an exception for this opponent.

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.550
You can’t defeat him on your own.

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:01.380
He’s that strong?

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:04.270
He’s unlike anyone you’ve fought before.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:06.160
Actually...

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.690
He’s also unlike anyone I’ve fought before.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:13.900
If you’re going that far, then I’m fired up!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:18.610
My goal is to become duel champion!

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.200
I’m kattobing!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.790
Duel mode! Photon change!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.450
What?

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:49.810
AR Vision Link complete.

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:53.520
I’m going to hunt.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.310
Including your soul!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.610
Duel!

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.170
I’ll go first.

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.450
My turn! I draw!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.920
I activate the spell card Photon Veil from my hand.

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:16.820
I return three LIGHT
monsters in my hand to my deck.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:20.590
Then I add three LIGHT
monsters in my deck to my hand.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.350
He exchanged three monsters.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:27.020
I activate the spell Photon Lead.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:35.020
I Special Summon a Level 4-or-below LIGHT monster that I added from my deck to my hand in attack position.

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:38.490
I Special Summon Daybreaker!

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:51.920
When this card is Special Summoned,
I can Special Summon a card with the same name from my hand.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.880
Appear, another Daybreaker!

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:59.380
The new Daybreaker’s effect activates.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.050
I Special Summon another Daybreaker!

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.870
He instantly has three monsters!

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:08.740
This is bad.

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:11.980
All the monsters on his field are Level 4!

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:12.980
That means...

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:17.190
I overlay three Level 4 Daybreakers!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.410
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:26.280
Xyz Summon!

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:34.840
Appear, Number 10: Illumiknight!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.480
Unbelievable!

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:46.260
He summoned a Number on his first turn.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.640
I’m not done.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:50.720
I activate Number 10: Illumiknight’s effect!

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:55.440
Illumiknight can use an Overlay Unit once per turn.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:21:00.840
I send one card in my hand to the graveyard to draw one card from my deck.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:05.280
Then the effect of Lightserpent that went to the graveyard activates.

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:10.700
When Lightserpent is sent from the hand to the graveyard,
it’s Special Summoned to the field.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.920
Then I Normal Summon Plasma Ball!

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.050
Again!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.840
He now has three monsters.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:29.620
How many monsters is he planning to summon?

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:30.310
Actually...

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:31.770
This is...

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:36.070
I overlay Level 3 Lightserpent and Plasma Ball!

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:40.770
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:41.690
Xyz Summon!

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.200
Appear, Number 20!

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:58.750
Giga-Brilliant!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.220
You must be kidding!

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:05.560
Two Numbers in one turn!

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:08.540
The hunt is about to begin.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:16.000
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.100
This week’s quiz:

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:22.140
Normally, up to how many monsters can you summon?

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:24.480
5 or 6?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:34.960
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:39.920
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:54.540
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:59.520
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:01.940
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:04.820
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:06.940
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.690
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:18.070
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:23.640
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.640 --> 00:23:28.130
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.280
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:37.230
Nothing is correct!

00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:44.400
He’s incredibly strong!

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:47.570
His dueling is superior to mine?

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:51.570
No way... I’m afraid to duel!

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:53.860
Yuma, overcome your fears!

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:57.120
We’ll combine our powers in this duel!

00:23:57.120 --> 00:23:59.660
With this, it’s over.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:01.460
Oh no!

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:06.800
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon Descends!”

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hGalaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon Descends!\h\h

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:10.010
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:14.340
The answer is... 5!

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:19.610
If you get 5 monsters, it must be really exciting!

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:24.150
I want to summon a lot of monsters and battle!
